From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avio: dhub: rate-limit "Spurious interrupt" log with delta
 counter

The AVIO DHUB ISR's "Spurious interrupt" message can be emitted at display
refresh rate (60-75 Hz) for the short race window between request_irq() in
drv_dhub_open and Dhub_IntrRegisterHandler() in the VPP path, where the AVIO
IRQ is live but the per-slot handler is not yet attached. On boots where the
window is wider than usual the console floods at ~120 lines/s and becomes
unusable.

Vendor (Synaptics) confirms the issue is non-functional - the ISR acks the
semaphore correctly even without a handler, the race window only spans early
boot, and downstream VPP consumers register vsync callbacks only after the
window closes so no events can be lost. Recommended remedy is to silence the
log.

Rather than fully downgrade to debug (which loses the diagnostic signal
entirely), gate the message with hand-rolled rate-limiting that:

  - emits the first occurrence immediately so a single boot-time race is
    visible at default loglevel
  - throttles subsequent occurrences to one log per 5 seconds, each carrying
    a delta (+N since last log) plus running total

This makes the difference between a benign race window (one or two messages
then silence as the handler attaches) and a true regression (heartbeat with
ever-growing total) immediately readable from a single dmesg snapshot,
without the flood.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
---
 .../soc/berlin/modules/avio/dhub/drv_dhub.c   | 24 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/synaptics/soc/berlin/modules/avio/dhub/drv_dhub.c b/drivers/synaptics/soc/berlin/modules/avio/dhub/drv_dhub.c
--- a/drivers/synaptics/soc/berlin/modules/avio/dhub/drv_dhub.c
+++ b/drivers/synaptics/soc/berlin/modules/avio/dhub/drv_dhub.c
@@ -213,10 +213,28 @@ static irqreturn_t avio_devices_dhub_isr(int irq, void *dev_id)
 		if (intr_status && p_int_handler->pIntrHandler)
 			p_int_handler->pIntrHandler(intr_status,
 				p_int_handler->pIntrHandlerArgs);
-		else
-			avio_error("%s:%d: Spurious interrupt - %d/%x/%x\n",
-				__func__, __LINE__, intr_num,
-				intr_status, p_int_handler->intrMask);
+		else {
+			static unsigned long spurious_total;
+			static unsigned long spurious_logged;
+			static unsigned long spurious_next_log;
+			spurious_total++;
+			if (spurious_total == 1) {
+				avio_error("%s:%d: Spurious interrupt - %d/%x/%x (first occurrence, total=%lu)\n",
+					__func__, __LINE__, intr_num,
+					intr_status, p_int_handler->intrMask,
+					spurious_total);
+				spurious_logged = spurious_total;
+				spurious_next_log = jiffies + 5 * HZ;
+			} else if (time_after(jiffies, spurious_next_log)) {
+				avio_error("%s:%d: Spurious interrupt - %d/%x/%x (+%lu since last, total=%lu)\n",
+					__func__, __LINE__, intr_num,
+					intr_status, p_int_handler->intrMask,
+					spurious_total - spurious_logged,
+					spurious_total);
+				spurious_logged = spurious_total;
+				spurious_next_log = jiffies + 5 * HZ;
+			}
+		}

 		//Clear the interrupt bit in instat
 		instat &= ~(1 << intr_num);
--
2.43.0

